            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Authors demonstrate 21 cases with primary dysmenorrhoea at girls aged 14-17 years, which were observed between 1989-1992 and present way of treatment. In their opinion administration of nonsteroid, antiphlogistic medicaments and the spasmolytics is the most effective method.</AbstractText>
